{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/992265-trying-to-understand-supernal-reality","id":992265,"title":"Trying to understand Supernal reality...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-23T22:16:13-07:00","id":992265,"title":"Trying to understand Supernal reality...","content":"Moderately recent CoD fan, and I'm enjoying pretty much every aspect of the cosmology, setting, and mechanics (particularly the God-Machine and the Shadow), but I've only recently entered the magical world of Awakening. It might be my near-complete lack of experience with all of the 1e books, but i need help understanding the Supernal, specifically 2e, and what content or books from 1e are still compatible so i can read them without misinterpreting current mechanics<br /> <br /> <br /> First things first; I don't understand how 2e specifically says that the Supernal is not a location, but rather the collective symbols and concepts that make up our world. If this is the case, how can a being be summoned from the various realms? My interpretation of the book is that these creatures have lives and minds outside of a given interaction, just like how, if i meet a spirit of anger, i can assume it will go back to feeding off of anger essence when i leave, as it had been doing before i arrived. Where does a Seraphim come from when it's summoned, and what happens to an Imp once my interaction with it ends?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12318-gaius94","user":"Gaius94","date":". 10-24-2016, 01:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12318-gaius94","name":"Gaius94","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T01:39:08-07:00","id":992299,"title":"","content":"<b>Personally, I like to picture Awakening as mass insanity that grants magic, in five versions. </b>Mages 'summons' their 'realms' rules that are common magical laws, bypassing those of Fallen World. Only those 'Laws' are totally unstable and can summon forces changing reality in ways he did not 'forseen it' ( i.e. Paradox ) and can run amok when he will not contain it. You know how this sound? Yes, it's sound like SuperPsychics. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> 2E marks that Paradox is really a problem of your own psyche could not restrain forces you unleash on world.<br /> <br /> <b>In nutshell, mages are Carrie or Charlene from horror movies with various powers, that can tap to occult Symbols for even more powers.</b> Magic being unstable as popculture media 'powers' is stempla of <b>Mage</b> 2E.<br /> <br /> And now we come to non-existing Supernal Realms. You see, mages, as insane superpsychics, can get even more powers by dwelling more in to their madness by imaging world as Symbols of Power, i.e. Active and Focused Mage Sight. <b>Imperial Mysteries</b> and lately <b>DaveB</b> confirms that Supernal Realms are immaterial and kills anyone trying to treat it as such. Here is his post on this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990170-question-about-supernal-realms-vs-other-realms?p=990325#post990325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The world isn't Fallen because it's not the Supernal - there was a world before the Fall - but because it's damaged by the Abyss.<br /> <br /> The Supernal Realm is not a physical place, and destroys anything that tries to treat it like one.<br /> <br /> Other supernatural beings have Supernal symbols over them when viewed in Mage Sight, but then so does *everything*. Mages don't believe vampires are linked to Stygia just because they show up in Death Sight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or that Supernal is <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/858922-mystery-supernal-is-%E2%80%98growing%E2%80%99-with-humanity\">evolving with humanity</a> - just see a topic I made on this meta-Mystery of setting and understand that Supernal is just collection of Symbols humanity describe as magical <b>now</b>.<br /> <br /> Also, nice thing to know is that in Time Before Fall, Supernal Realms were fourth layer of Astral! You just needed to mediate very hard to get there. Now there is Abyss in this place in Astral, but it's like they were just moved beyond starting pool. Basically, whole Supernal Magic is supergoetia of Astral Realms moved outside of normal reality, still evolving with humanity!<br /> <br /> So we asserted that Supernal Realms are just supercollection of Symbols that can grant magical abilities ( because they are cosmic madness spreading from outside of Astral ). <b>Now how then Awakened can summon Fae, Angels or Beasts if they are not coming from physical realms? </b>Simple - mages create 'bodies' from their Path Arcana. You see how Supernal Summoning need at least 3 dots in Ruling Arcanum? And what we have on as Practices on 3rd dot? Weaving, Practice of transforming things. In nurshell, Supernal Summoning is hammering Supernal Symbol ( i.e. portion of Paths madness ) into body made of stuff from this Arcanum.<br /> <br /> <b>Supernal Summoning is, in reality, summoning Supergoetia about Arcana, not normal Astral stuff!</b> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And because we talk about fleeting cosmic madness that Fallen reality does not want in it's neighborhood, Supernal beings cannot stay in Fallen World more than few hours. <b>Contrary to spirits or ghosts, they are only visualizations of mage psyche about his cosmic powers, not reflecting natural phenomena or once living people, so their 'anchor' is much weaker and they naturally erase from it. </b>&lt;Banisher talk&gt; Supernal is madness and should be banished from reality! &lt;/Banisher talk&gt;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-24-2016, 04:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T03:39:15-07:00","id":992319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990754-question-about-the-supernal-beings\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990754-question-about-the-supernal-beings\"> Question About The Supernal Beings - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990754-question-about-the-supernal-beings\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990754-question-about-the-supernal-beings </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Can they exist at the same in more than one realm in Second edition? I know Imperial Mysteries mentioned they could. Na example they Gave was the Hunter In Green. An supernal god representing predation. The Hunter exists in both Stygia and Primal Wild. At least that's what i remember. Is that still holds true in this new edtition? Also a somewhat related question. i start wondering something when i read that sidebar on dark eras &amp;quot;Generations of sorcery have given some magical environments and Verges stronger but more specific Supernal ties than usual. To take advantage of such places, </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}